comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-18T12:39:32.158Z",codex-gpt5,"GitHub report evidence 2026-07-18: open Scorecard CIIBestPracticesID alert #22 is low severity on refs/heads/main with no file-specific location. Canonical remediation remains this item; no duplicate created."
  "2026-07-26T09:09:15.756Z","harness:codex","Repository-side preparation complete: the PM note contains a current passing-criteria evidence matrix and explicit maintainer confirmations. Registration and attestation at bestpractices.dev remain maintainer-controlled external actions; no badge is claimed before the service records a real project status."
  "2026-07-26T09:11:10.786Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: the maintainer-controlled attestation boundary and prepared evidence matrix ship in PR #735 at head 39acfef6; item remains open and unclaimed pending authorized bestpractices.dev submission."
  "2026-07-26T11:32:40.173Z","harness:claude-code","Live Scorecard alert state 2026-07-26: code-scanning alert #22 (CIIBestPracticesID, severity low) is open and is this item's meter. Registration remains human-gated; recorded here so the alert is traceable to an owner rather than re-triaged each pass."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T08:57:38.733Z","harness:codex","Draft passing-questionnaire evidence matrix for maintainer confirmation and submission:\n- Basics=yes: README describes pm-cli, npm/GitHub provide stable obtain URLs, GitHub Issues provides feedback, CONTRIBUTING documents PRs and acceptance gates, MIT LICENSE is OSI-compatible.\n- Change control=yes: public git history, date-based unique versions, generated CHANGELOG, GitHub releases, npm artifacts, and release verification are public.\n- Documentation=yes: README quickstart, docs index, command help/contracts, SDK/extension guides, architecture, testing, contribution, code of conduct, and security policy are linked.\n- Defect/security reporting=yes after this bundle: public issue tracker for normal defects; GitHub private vulnerability reporting URL, response targets, coordinated disclosure, scope, and safe harbor in SECURITY.md.\n- Build/quality=yes: Node and pnpm prerequisites, reproducible install/build commands, TypeScript strict typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, CodeFactor-calibrated static gate, ShellCheck/PSScriptAnalyzer/actionlint, CodeQL/Semgrep/Trivy/TruffleHog, and warnings-as-errors CI.\n- Tests=yes: public Vitest suite, required 100% statements/branches/functions/lines, cross-platform/runtime/installed-package lanes, and fast-check property fuzzing of four trust boundaries on every PR.\n- Dependencies=yes: lockfile, Dependabot, pnpm audit, pinned GitHub Actions, engine-aware upgrade dispositions, and published-package consumer verification.\n- Secure development=yes based on repository evidence: private reports are isolated, secrets are scanned/redacted, extension trust boundaries are documented, telemetry is redacted, mutations/history are integrity checked, and releases use provenance-aware npm/GitHub workflows.\n- Crypto=standard-library only: SHA-256 hashing and platform/package cryptographic primitives are not custom cryptographic protocols; maintainer should confirm the questionnaire N/A/yes selections.\n- Maintainer confirmations required before submission: project is actively maintained; all MUST answers remain accurate; SHOULD exceptions have truthful justifications; no known undisclosed vulnerability contradicts an answer; private vulnerability reporting is enabled; submitter is authorized to attest for unbraind.\n- After bestpractices.dev returns a project id/status, record the public URL here and add the official badge to README only when the service reports in-progress or passing as appropriate."
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
